1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,600
Could this be...

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:04,960
Isn't it obvious?

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,160
A mixer at a karaoke bar.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,040
Because he's so sweet.

5
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:10,040
For my sake.

6
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:15,410
Maybe one day he'll feel obligated to like me,
or he'll start walking on eggshells around me.

7
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:20,280
That's not the kind of
feelings I want from him.

8
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:24,089
Why don't you just show him
this side of you, too?

9
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:25,550
Everything you just said,

10
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,790
and all those messy thoughts in your head.

11
00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:31,660
If you just tell him honestly,
he'll definitely understand.

12
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:34,900
What misunderstanding...
are you talking about?

13
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,830
If Mayama doesn't actually like me,

14
00:00:38,930 --> 00:00:41,870
but forces himself to out of consideration
for me, that would really hurt.

15
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:43,570
I still want...

16
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:48,140
to spend more time with Mayama.

17
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:51,580
Your "like"...

18
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,520
What kind of "like" is it?

19
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:00,660
I want to touch you.

20
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,890
I want to hold your hand.

21
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,600
I want to hug you.

22
00:01:08,230 --> 00:01:09,630
It's that kind of "like."

23
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:27,350
I can't wait to see you.

24
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:28,750
Kou-chan.

25
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,499
(Good morning.) (Are you still sleeping?)
(I dreamt about Mayama.)

26
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,700
(What time are you leaving today?)
(You've read the messages.) (Good morning.)

27
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,340
I'm heading out.

28
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:40,920
Hello.
I'm your boyfriend.

29
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,490
I know.

30
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,890
Then who might this be?

31
00:02:46,230 --> 00:02:47,430
I'm your boyfriend.

32
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:50,930
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

33
00:02:58,710 --> 00:03:00,280
What time do you work until today?

34
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,680
With data entry, I'll be done by evening.

35
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:05,410
I'm sorry.

36
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:07,220
Huh?

37
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:09,550
We just started dating, too.

38
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:12,810
Then I'll wait for you to get off work.

39
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,300
Okay.

40
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,830
It's so strange.

41
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,960
Hmm?

42
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,400
I thought I had already liked you
past my absolute limit.

43
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:26,200
But after we started dating,
I like you even more than before.

44
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:29,810
Oh my.

45
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:33,510
I don't even know how to respond to that...

46
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:36,010
Am I coming on too strong?

47
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,879
Huh? No, not at all.

48
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,479
Let me carry your bag.

49
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:41,480
Ah...

50
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:44,420
Thanks.

51
00:03:45,290 --> 00:03:46,990
I need to rack up those boyfriend points.

52
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:50,360
Ten points gets me a kiss.

53
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:17,020
You can just drop me off here.

54
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:26,030
I'm walking you in. It's not trespassing.

55
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,080
Honestly...

56
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:45,310
Recharging my energy.

57
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:47,020
So I can make it through to the evening.

58
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:50,520
Am I an energy drink or something?

59
00:04:54,590 --> 00:04:55,590
Mayama.

60
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:57,660
Right now?

61
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,260
Right now.

62
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:11,510
I'll come pick you up this evening.

63
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:14,510
Okay, see you later.

64
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,360
I'm going in.

65
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:34,260
That's totally unfair.

66
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:24,700
"After Moving Seats, The Boy Behind Me Has A Crush On Me"
(Episode 7)

67
00:06:30,150 --> 00:06:31,150
Thank you.

68
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:36,060
Are you free this Saturday?

69
00:06:36,450 --> 00:06:37,450
Huh?

70
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:40,940
Well...

71
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,600
The Tanabata Festival...

72
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:49,299
It's held near your hometown, right?

73
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:50,300
Yeah.

74
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:53,880
It's already that time of year.

75
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:57,780
Do you want to go together?

76
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:01,380
Uh...

77
00:07:03,650 --> 00:07:04,350
You can't?

78
00:07:04,351 --> 00:07:05,890
It's not that I can't.

79
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:08,960
It's just...

80
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:12,060
I knew it. I actually have a shift
as event staff that day.

81
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,230
I see.

82
00:07:13,231 --> 00:07:16,179
But I'm off the next day,
so we could find another festival...

83
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:17,800
But that's the only day I'm free.

84
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:18,680
Huh?

85
00:07:18,681 --> 00:07:21,340
I have summer classes
for a while after that.

86
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:26,580
At this rate, I'm going to have a
severe Mayama energy deficiency.

87
00:07:28,810 --> 00:07:29,810
Sorry.

88
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:32,510
No, I'm sorry too.

89
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:42,520
It would be nice if we could do
something summery.

90
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,800
Ma-chan.

91
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:16,460
You can go take a break in the back.

92
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:22,299
Good work.

93
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,930
Good work.

94
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,569
It's way too hot...

95
00:08:26,570 --> 00:08:28,040
It really is.

96
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,679
Here, have some water.

97
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,680
Thanks.

98
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:37,010
I didn't expect the event job
to be the Tanabata Festival.

99
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:42,860
Next, could you walk around the venue
and hand out wish strips?

100
00:08:42,890 --> 00:08:43,420
Sure.

101
00:08:43,421 --> 00:08:45,599
You're a lifesaver.

102
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,639
Isn't it insanely hot out?

103
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:50,280
Nobody wants to wear the mascot suit.

104
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:52,230
But someone has to do it.

105
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:54,760
You taking on this job
really saved us.

106
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:57,170
What should we do with
the wish strips over there?

107
00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:01,840
So it's this festival.

108
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,070
What are you talking about?

109
00:09:07,010 --> 00:09:10,480
Hey, hey, we were obviously joking.

110
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,920
There's no way she'd ever like Mayama.

111
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:23,460
It brings back bad memories.

112
00:09:40,010 --> 00:09:41,540
Asamiya?

113
00:09:52,490 --> 00:09:54,320
Why is Asamiya here?

114
00:09:54,590 --> 00:09:56,860
Didn't I say I couldn't go with him?

115
00:09:57,730 --> 00:09:59,830
Kou-chan, Kou-chan.

116
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:03,359
Kou-chan, honestly.

117
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,939
Stop leaving me behind.

118
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:05,940
Huh?

119
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,700
What?

120
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,480
It talks!

121
00:10:16,510 --> 00:10:18,250
It's better to go inside.

122
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:22,250
Oh, do you want a wish strip?

123
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:23,990
I'm good.

124
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:26,520
You're so uncooperative, honestly.

125
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,690
Oh, excuse me.

126
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,060
Could I get a wish strip, please?

127
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,560
Hmm?

128
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:38,970
Um... hi...?

129
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:42,040
Huh?

130
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:43,200
Ah.

131
00:10:44,010 --> 00:10:45,440
Thank you.

132
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,880
Don't you feel an intense, oppressive vibe?

133
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,050
You're overthinking it.

134
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:51,450
I see.

135
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,526
Alright, let's go check
out the stalls. The stalls!

136
00:10:53,550 --> 00:10:55,780
I kind of want some shaved ice.

137
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,250
- Do you want some?
- No thanks.

138
00:11:04,430 --> 00:11:06,860
Festivals really are the best.

139
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,200
It feels like I'm finally back in Japan.

140
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:11,680
Thank you.

141
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:13,070
For coming with me.

142
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:20,040
What's the relationship
between that person and Asamiya?

143
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:25,150
When I was studying abroad, I was constantly
thinking about how you were doing.

144
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:26,760
Oh...

145
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:37,890
Is it still there?

146
00:11:37,890 --> 00:11:38,890
Yeah.

147
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:39,960
Right behind us.

148
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:41,560
Staring right at us.

149
00:12:11,630 --> 00:12:16,900
He was just using me to fill the void
while his girlfriend was studying abroad.

150
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,640
Was I just a backup?

151
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:31,310
I've also seen a lot of things
that Mayama feels insecure about.

152
00:12:33,650 --> 00:12:38,120
But I've only grown to
like you more, Mayama.

153
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:43,790
Romantically, of course.

154
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,240
Asamiya would never do something like that.

155
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:56,070
I need to make sure of this.

156
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,199
Well, well, if it isn't Mayama.

157
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,339
Whoa.

158
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:01,380
Kagami...

159
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:03,080
Long time no see.

160
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,279
Hey, what's with the getup?

161
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:06,750
That's ridiculous.

162
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:09,500
Is it still there?

163
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:13,790
Yeah.

164
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,120
It's fine now.

165
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:19,560
What's with the sigh?
Don't sigh at me.

166
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:22,540
You can't just easily get
a girlfriend this cute, you know.

167
00:13:22,970 --> 00:13:24,410
You really think highly of yourself.

168
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,670
By the way,
that person in the mascot suit earlier...

169
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,680
That looks rough.

170
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:29,400
Wearing that in this heat.

171
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:33,680
I actually know someone who
would volunteer for a job like that.

172
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:35,340
Hmm?

173
00:13:41,850 --> 00:13:43,289
Seriously? This is the guy?

174
00:13:43,290 --> 00:13:46,289
The legendary target of
the fake confession prank.

175
00:13:46,290 --> 00:13:48,920
I almost died laughing back then.

176
00:13:51,156 --> 00:13:54,376
Anyway, working at the place where you got
pranked takes some serious mental fortitude.

177
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,430
Tell me about it.

178
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,670
Hey, why are you so down?

179
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:00,680
It's nothing.

180
00:14:00,681 --> 00:14:02,079
You should go on a date with Mayama.

181
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:03,339
Why?

182
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:05,199
I want to cheer Mayama up.

183
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,339
What?

184
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:09,380
I'm seeing someone now, after all.

185
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:10,850
Mayama is seeing someone?

186
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:12,449
That's definitely a lie.

187
00:14:12,450 --> 00:14:13,450
It's a lie, right?

188
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:15,380
Go on.

189
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:17,419
Don't be shy.

190
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,860
Just take a lap around the venue.

191
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:21,809
Shall we go, then?

192
00:14:21,810 --> 00:14:22,810
Go, go.

193
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
I think I'll...

194
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:27,700
What?

195
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,720
You're really uncooperative.

196
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:33,700
- Hurry up and go.
- Yeah.

197
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:34,760
Go on.

198
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:37,270
No.

199
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:38,410
What?

200
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:39,780
I don't want to go.

201
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,780
Huh?

202
00:14:42,710 --> 00:14:45,050
You guys always say it's
just a prank, just a joke.

203
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:48,450
But I actually really hate it.

204
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:52,239
I don't want anything to do with you
or the rest of your gang anymore, Kagami.

205
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,860
Huh? What's your problem?

206
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,130
You little...

207
00:14:57,590 --> 00:14:59,630
You don't have any other friends
besides us, do you?

208
00:15:02,930 --> 00:15:07,700
I have friends now who stay by my side
without me having to do that kind of stuff.

209
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,610
Just go when I tell you to.

210
00:15:22,850 --> 00:15:24,250
Don't touch Mayama.

211
00:15:24,950 --> 00:15:26,250
Who do you think you are?

212
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,030
I'm Mayama's friend.

213
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:31,659
Unlike you guys.

214
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:32,660
Huh?

215
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:36,630
Ow!

216
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,170
That hurts!

217
00:15:40,170 --> 00:15:42,070
Don't you ever come near Mayama again.

218
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,340
Let's go.

219
00:16:01,590 --> 00:16:02,590
Mayama.

220
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:08,000
Thank goodness...

221
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,320
Thank you.

222
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:16,680
No.

223
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,320
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

224
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:20,140
I should've noticed sooner.

225
00:16:27,350 --> 00:16:29,950
Did I earn some boyfriend points for that?

226
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:35,190
Mayama?

227
00:16:39,980 --> 00:16:41,130
That person from earlier...

228
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,940
Huh?

229
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,500
I saw you.

230
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:55,340
I saw you walking arm in arm
with a really pretty girl.

231
00:16:56,810 --> 00:16:57,950
That was...

232
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,310
Kou-chan!

233
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:01,680
Geez.
So this is where you were, Kou-chan.

234
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,219
I've been looking all over for you.

235
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:04,990
Where did you run off to?

236
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:08,120
Hm?

237
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:10,000
Who's this?

238
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,230
My friend, Mayama.

239
00:17:16,830 --> 00:17:18,550
Thanks for always looking out for Kou-chan.

240
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,200
I'm his older sister, Asamiya Koiro.

241
00:17:24,470 --> 00:17:25,470
Huh?

242
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:31,410
Older sister?

243
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:33,160
We don't look much alike, do we?

244
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:36,050
But you were walking arm in arm earlier...

245
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:39,390
There's this girl who's
been pestering me lately.

246
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,760
She followed me all
the way here today, so...

247
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:45,190
Yeah. So I stepped in to play
Kou-chan's girlfriend for a bit.

248
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:49,460
I didn't expect you to
be the one to see us.

249
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,370
So that's what happened...

250
00:17:56,470 --> 00:17:59,070
You're Mayama, right?

251
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:00,480
Yes.

252
00:18:04,510 --> 00:18:05,950
Please take good care of my brother.

253
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:07,980
Ah.

254
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:10,599
Though Kou-chan can be pretty clingy.

255
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:11,600
Ah... No, he's not...

256
00:18:11,650 --> 00:18:12,620
You don't need to say all that.

257
00:18:12,621 --> 00:18:13,979
Ah, sorry, sorry.

258
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:14,980
Oh, right.

259
00:18:18,690 --> 00:18:19,800
- Here.
- Hm?

260
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:20,860
For you.

261
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:23,000
Why don't you guys write one too?

262
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:28,000
Alright, that's it for me.

263
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:30,310
Run along now.

264
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,650
What did you write?

265
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:39,560
Hmm, I'm not telling.

266
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,490
Where do you want to hang it?

267
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,370
What did you write?

268
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:58,170
It's a secret.

269
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:00,760
I feel like it won't come
true if I say it out loud.

270
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,710
Then mine's a secret too.

271
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:12,980
The grand finale fireworks of the
Tanabata Festival are about to begin.

272
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:17,420
Please enjoy this wonderful
summer memory together.

273
00:19:18,590 --> 00:19:20,020
I didn't know there'd be fireworks.

274
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:23,090
- Follow me.
- Huh?

275
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:25,260
This is my turf.

276
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,670
Wait...

277
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:34,400
You're walking too fast...

278
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:36,040
Are we still going?

279
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:40,540
No... We're here.

280
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:44,250
Look.

281
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,880
Wow...

282
00:19:52,190 --> 00:19:55,760
Back when I was pranked
with that fake confession,

283
00:19:56,990 --> 00:19:59,490
I ran away crying to this exact spot.

284
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:08,800
At the time, these
fireworks kind of saved me.

285
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:21,320
Doesn't it hurt to think about it now?

286
00:20:28,890 --> 00:20:31,050
Not anymore, because you're
here with me, Asamiya-kun.

287
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:42,540
I mean...

288
00:20:42,770 --> 00:20:44,570
Let's watch the fireworks.

289
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,780
I'm so glad.

290
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:52,510
We finally did something summery.

291
00:20:55,710 --> 00:20:56,710
Yeah.

292
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:56,699
(I hope Mayama finds happiness.)

293
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:01,700
(I hope to find happiness
together with Asamiya-kun.)

294
00:22:23,010 --> 00:22:27,180
My sister said she's crashing
at a friend's place tonight.

295
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:30,800
Yeah.

296
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:35,920
My parents are out on a trip too,
so they won't be home.

297
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:44,090
Do you want to come over?

298
00:22:46,430 --> 00:22:47,430
Huh...

299
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:49,900
You don't want to?

300
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:57,270
It's not that I don't want to... but...

301
00:23:00,780 --> 00:23:04,010
I just... don't want to let
you go home yet tonight.

302
00:24:28,030 --> 00:24:31,770
(Next Episode) I feel like the
limiter on my heart has been taken off.

303
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:36,100
Can't we tell Sakaki
and the others about us?

304
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:37,110
Keeping it a secret like this...

305
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:37,870
It's probably best if we don't.

306
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:39,540
Someone might see us.

307
00:24:39,780 --> 00:24:42,340
You never used to care about
this kind of stuff before, did you?

308
00:24:42,510 --> 00:24:45,750
My romance with Asamiya-kun
that started...

309
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:47,240
- That day...
- Asamiya-kun.

310
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:50,490
This romance that
started from moving seats...

311
00:24:51,340 --> 00:24:54,620
Are you really okay with this, Asamiya-kun?
